  "design_section": "7.2.1",
  "design_notes": [
    "The table is headed \"Instrument (C1 Earth Watch)\", so every option lists C1 only.",
    "The table has no Strengths column. The remarks in the Science value cell (\"wildfires, ice\"; \"sees through clouds, at night\") are carried as strengths; the other two options have none.",
    "power_duty is set only for the radar (\"300 W during imaging\"). The other three cells give a bare wattage; the suggested loader default is continuous. requires_cooling is set only where the Power cell says \"needs cooling\".",
    "sees_through_clouds and works_at_night are set only where the design states them: false for the wide-field camera (its drawback), true for the radar (its Science value cell).",
    "No provenance is stated for instrument mass, power and data figures; table 5.1 calls the payload a game value and 7.17 calls data rates game values, so stats are tagged game_value.",
    "Rules shared by all four: MG-05 Clean Room runs at \"science payload integration\", MG-21 Science Capture is the instrument at work (it treats radar differently), and section 6.8 weights Contamination in Clean Room towards science payloads. No weight multiplier is given.",
    "facts: F16 (Landsat) is stated in the multispectral row and is the fact of MG-21, which every instrument enables, so all four carry it.",
    "\"High data volume needs a strong radio\" (multispectral) names no radio; it is enforced by the data-budget rule of 6.11 through data_GB_per_day, so there is no requires_part rule.",
    "The table gives no lead time, integration days or reliability."
  ],
